# `held.run?.(1)`: the read of the method hands the callee back in the register of results, and the receiver waits in the register in which the read took it.
# The convention of calls wants the callee and `this` elsewhere. The stub that calls by value brings both there in front of its entry: the place holds neither move.
# RUN: bytes f1:Body mechanisms=all-Inlining
# REQUIRES: x86_64
# CHECK: Call Stub CallValue.Ordinary count 1, entered in front of two moves

